{"book": "gate-da", "num": 21, "label": "21", "slug": "21-calculus-limits", "title": "Limits", "tag": "Calculus & Optimization", "summary": "Calculus emerged from the need to solve practical problems in physics and engineering. Two fundamental problems led to its development:", "wordCount": 1311, "readingTimeMin": 7, "intro": [], "sections": [{"id": "21.1", "title": "Introduction to Calculus", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Calculus emerged from the need to solve practical problems in physics and engineering. Two fundamental problems led to its development:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>The Tangent Problem</b>: Determining the slope of a line tangent to a curve at a given point."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>The Area Problem</b>: Calculating the area under a curve."}]}]}]}, {"id": "21.2", "title": "The Tangent Problem and Differential Calculus", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The rate of change is a critical concept in calculus. To understand this, consider the graphs of the following linear functions:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$f(x) = -2x - 3$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$g(x) = \\frac{x}{2} + 1$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$h(x) = 2$"}]}]}, {"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/calc/fig023.png"], "caption": "Graphs of linear functions with constant rates of change."}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The slope of a linear function indicates the rate of change. For example:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$f(x) = -2x - 3$: slope = -2"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$g(x) = \\frac{x}{2} + 1$: slope = 1/2"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$h(x) = 2$: slope = 0"}]}]}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "Now consider the quadratic function $k(x) = x^2$. Its rate of change is not constant. To approximate it, we use secant lines."}, {"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/calc/fig024.png"], "caption": "Graph of $k(x) = x^2$ with a secant line."}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A <b>secant line</b> to a function $f(x)$ through points $(a, f(a))$ and $(x, f(x))$ passes through these points. Its slope is"}, {"t": "math", "x": "m_{\\text{sec}} = \\frac{f(x) - f(a)}{x - a}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "As $x$ approaches $a$, the secant line approaches the tangent line. Its slope approaches the derivative of $f(x)$ at $a$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "28", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Find the slope of the secant line to $k(x) = x^2$ through points $(1,1)$ and $(2,4)$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "m_{\\text{sec}} = \\frac{4-1}{2-1} = 3."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The slope of the tangent line at a point gives the instantaneous rate of change, which is the derivative of the function at that point."}]}]}, {"id": "21.3", "title": "The Area Problem and Integral Calculus", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "To find the area under a curve, approximate by summing rectangles."}, {"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/calc/fig025.png"], "caption": "Approximation of the area under $f(x) = x^2 + 1$ using rectangles."}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The <b>area under a curve</b> is approximated by summing the areas of rectangles over subintervals. As the width of the rectangles decreases, the sum approaches the exact area. This process leads to the definite integral."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "29", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Estimate the area under $f(x) = x^2 + 1$ over $[0,3]$ using three rectangles:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Area} \\approx \\sum_{i=1}^{3} \\text{Area of Rectangle}_i"}]}]}, {"id": "21.4", "title": "Conclusion", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The Tangent and Area Problems lead to the foundations of calculus:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Tangent Problem $\\rightarrow$ Derivative (rate of change)"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Area Problem $\\rightarrow$ Integral (area under curve)"}]}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "These concepts are essential for further studies in calculus and multivariable calculus."}]}, {"id": "21.5", "title": "Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Definition of a Limit", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "We say the <b>limit</b> of $f(x)$ is $L$ as $x$ approaches $a$ and write"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = L"}, {"t": "p", "x": "provided we can make $f(x)$ as close to $L$ as we want for all $x$ sufficiently close to $a$, from both sides, without actually letting $x=a$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Intuitive Idea", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The limit describes the behavior of $f(x)$ around $x=a$, not necessarily the value at $x=a$. As $x$ approaches $a$, $f(x)$ must move closer and closer to $L$. This must hold for values of $x$ on both sides of $a$."}]}]}, {"id": "21.6", "title": "Estimating Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "To estimate limits, we examine the behavior of a function as $x$ approaches a point $a$ from both sides. The idea is to find a value $X$ such that whenever $|x-a| < X$, the function's value $f(x)$ stays within a desired tolerance of the limit $L$."}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "30", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Estimate"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 3} \\frac{x^2 + 5x - 18}{x^2 - 3x}."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Observation", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Although the function is undefined at $x=3$, we can study its behavior for values near 3."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "31", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Define"}, {"t": "math", "x": "g(x) =\n\\begin{cases}\n\\dfrac{x^2 + 5x - 18}{x^2 - 3x}, & x \\neq 3\\\\\n7, & x=3\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Estimate $\\lim_{x \\to 3} g(x)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Answer:</b> As in Example 1, the limit is 4, even though $g(3) = 7$.\nThis shows that limits depend on nearby values of $x$, not the function's value at the point itself."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "32", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Estimate"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0} \\frac{1 - \\cos(2\\theta)}{\\theta}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Observation:</b> The function is undefined at $\\theta = 0$, but by evaluating values close to 0, we can approximate the limit."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "33", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Estimate"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{t \\to 0} \\sin(\\pi t/2)."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Observation:</b> Tables of values may help, but they can be misleading. Graphical analysis or algebraic methods provide more reliable estimates."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "34", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Estimate"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{t \\to 0} X(t), \\quad X(t) =\n\\begin{cases}\n-1, & t<0\\\\\n2, & t \\ge 0\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Observation:</b> Not all limits exist. Here, the left-hand limit is $-1$ and the right-hand limit is 2, so the limit does not exist."}]}]}, {"id": "21.7", "title": "Summary", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Key Points", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Limits describe the behavior of a function around a point, not necessarily the function's value at that point."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Limits can exist even if the function does not exist at that point."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A function can exist at a point, but its limit at that point might be different."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Tables and graphs can help understand limits but are not always reliable for exact values."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Some limits do not exist."}]}]}]}]}, {"id": "21.8", "title": "One-Sided Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "In the previous section, we saw two limits that did not exist for different reasons:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\displaystyle \\lim_{t \\to 0} \\cos(\\pi t)$ does not exist because the function oscillates and does not settle to a single value near $t=0$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\displaystyle \\lim_{t \\to 0} X(t), \\quad X(t)=\\begin{cases}0,& t<0\\\\1,& t\\ge 0\\end{cases}$ does not exist because the left-hand and right-hand limits are different."}]}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "To distinguish these situations, we introduce <b>one-sided limits</b>."}]}, {"id": "21.9", "title": "Definitions: One-Sided Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Right-Hand Limit", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "We say"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a^+} f(x) = L"}, {"t": "p", "x": "if we can make $f(x)$ as close to $L$ as desired for all $x>a$ sufficiently close to $a$, without considering $x=a$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Left-Hand Limit", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "We say"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a^-} f(x) = L"}, {"t": "p", "x": "if we can make $f(x)$ as close to $L$ as desired for all $x<a$ sufficiently close to $a$, without considering $x=a$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Observation", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The only difference between one-sided limits and ordinary limits is the direction from which $x$ approaches $a$. For a one-sided limit to exist, the function must approach a unique value from that side."}]}]}, {"id": "21.10", "title": "Examples", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "35", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Estimate:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{t \\to 0^+} H(t) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\lim_{t \\to 0^-} H(t), \\quad H(t)=\\begin{cases}0,& t<0\\\\1,& t\\ge 0\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{t \\to 0^+} H(t) = 1, \\quad \\lim_{t \\to 0^-} H(t) = 0"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "36", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Estimate:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{t \\to 0^+} \\sin\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\lim_{t \\to 0^-} \\sin\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Observation:</b> The function oscillates infinitely near $t=0$, so the one-sided limits do not exist."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "37", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let"}, {"t": "math", "x": "g(x) = \n\\begin{cases}\n\\dfrac{x^2 + 5x -18}{x^2 -3x}, & x\\neq 3\\\\\n7, & x=3\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Estimate:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 3^+} g(x) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\lim_{x \\to 3^-} g(x)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Both one-sided limits exist and equal 4."}]}]}, {"id": "21.11", "title": "Fact Relating One-Sided and Ordinary Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Fact", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "For a function $f(x)$:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $\\lim_{x \\to a^+} f(x) = \\lim_{x \\to a^-} f(x) = L$, then $\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = L$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Conversely, if $\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = L$, both one-sided limits exist and equal $L$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $\\lim_{x \\to a^+} f(x) \\neq \\lim_{x \\to a^-} f(x)$, then $\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)$ does not exist."}]}]}]}]}, {"id": "21.12", "title": "Properties of Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Properties of Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)$ and $\\lim_{x \\to a} g(x)$ exist, and let $c$ be any constant. Then the following properties hold:"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>1. Constant Multiple:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} [c f(x)] = c \\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<i>Example:</i> $\\lim_{x \\to 2} 4x^2 = 4 \\cdot 4 = 16$"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>2. Sum/Difference:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} [f(x) \\pm g(x)] = \\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) \\pm \\lim_{x \\to a} g(x)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<i>Example:</i> $\\lim_{x \\to 1} (x^2 + 3x) = 1 + 3 = 4$"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>3. Product:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} [f(x) g(x)] = \\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) \\cdot \\lim_{x \\to a} g(x)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<i>Example:</i> $\\lim_{x \\to 2} (x^2 \\cdot (x+1)) = 4 \\cdot 3 = 12$"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>4. Quotient:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} \\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} = \\frac{\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)}{\\lim_{x \\to a} g(x)}, \\quad \\lim_{x \\to a} g(x) \\neq 0"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<i>Example:</i> $\\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{x^2-4}{x-2} = \\lim_{x \\to 2} (x+2) = 4$"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>5. Power:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} [f(x)]^n = [\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)]^n"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<i>Example:</i> $\\lim_{x \\to 3} (x-1)^3 = 2^3 = 8$"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>6. Root:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} \\sqrt[n]{f(x)} = \\sqrt[n]{\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<i>Example:</i> $\\lim_{x \\to 9} \\sqrt{x} = 3$"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>7. Constant Function:</b> $\\lim_{x \\to a} c = c$"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>8. Identity Function:</b> $\\lim_{x \\to a} x = a$"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>9. Power of Identity:</b> $\\lim_{x \\to a} x^n = a^n$"}]}]}, {"id": "21.13", "title": "Infinite Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "In this section we study limits whose value is $\\infty$ or $-\\infty$. These limits appear frequently in calculus and other exams, so understanding them is essential."}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Definition of Infinite Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "We say"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = \\infty"}, {"t": "p", "x": "if we can make $f(x)$ arbitrarily large for all $x$ sufficiently close to $a$ (from both sides) without actually letting $x = a$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Similarly,"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = -\\infty"}, {"t": "p", "x": "if we can make $f(x)$ arbitrarily large and negative for all $x$ sufficiently close to $a$ without letting $x = a$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "These definitions can be extended to one-sided limits as well."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Vertical Asymptote", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A function $f(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x = a$ if any of the following limits is true:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a^-} f(x) = \\pm \\infty, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to a^+} f(x) = \\pm \\infty, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = \\pm \\infty"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Note: Only one of the above needs to hold."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "nuance", "name": "Fact", "num": null, "title": "Facts About Infinite Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be functions such that"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to c} f(x) = \\infty, \\quad \\lim_{x \\to c} g(x) = L"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Then:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to c} [f(x) \\pm g(x)] = \\infty"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to c} [f(x) g(x)] =\n\\begin{cases}\n\\infty & \\text{if } L > 0\\\\\n-\\infty & \\text{if } L < 0\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to c} \\frac{g(x)}{f(x)} = 0"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "38", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate the following limits:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} \\frac{1}{x}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to 0^-} \\frac{1}{x}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{1}{x}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- As $x \\to 0^+$, $x>0$ so $\\frac{1}{x} \\to +\\infty$.\n- As $x \\to 0^-$, $x<0$ so $\\frac{1}{x} \\to -\\infty$.\n- Since the left and right limits are not equal, $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{1}{x}$ does not exist."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "39", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate the following limits:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} \\frac{6}{x^2}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to 0^-} \\frac{6}{x^2}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{6}{x^2}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- As $x \\to 0$, $x^2>0$ so $\\frac{6}{x^2} \\to +\\infty$ from both sides.\n- Therefore, $\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} \\frac{6}{x^2} = \\lim_{x \\to 0^-} \\frac{6}{x^2} = \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{6}{x^2} = +\\infty$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "40", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate the following limits:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to -2^+} \\frac{-4}{x+2}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to -2^-} \\frac{-4}{x+2}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to -2} \\frac{-4}{x+2}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- As $x \\to -2^+$, $x+2>0$ so $\\frac{-4}{x+2} \\to -\\infty$.\n- As $x \\to -2^-$, $x+2<0$ so $\\frac{-4}{x+2} \\to +\\infty$.\n- Left and right limits are not equal, so the limit at $x=-2$ does not exist."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "41", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate the following limits:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\frac{3}{(4-x)^3}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to 4^-} \\frac{3}{(4-x)^3}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to 4} \\frac{3}{(4-x)^3}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- As $x \\to 4^+$, $4-x < 0$, so $(4-x)^3 <0$ and $\\frac{3}{(4-x)^3} \\to -\\infty$.\n- As $x \\to 4^-$, $4-x >0$, so $\\frac{3}{(4-x)^3} \\to +\\infty$.\n- Since left and right limits differ, $\\lim_{x \\to 4} \\frac{3}{(4-x)^3}$ does not exist."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "42", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate the following limits:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 3^+} \\frac{2x}{x-3}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to 3^-} \\frac{2x}{x-3}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to 3} \\frac{2x}{x-3}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- As $x \\to 3^+$, $x-3>0$ so $\\frac{2x}{x-3} \\to +\\infty$.\n- As $x \\to 3^-$, $x-3<0$ so $\\frac{2x}{x-3} \\to -\\infty$.\n- Left and right limits differ, so $\\lim_{x \\to 3} \\frac{2x}{x-3}$ does not exist."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "43", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate the one-sided limit:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} \\ln x"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- As $x \\to 0^+$, $\\ln x \\to -\\infty$.\n- So, $\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} \\ln x = -\\infty$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "44", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate the following limits:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\pi/2^+} \\tan x, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to \\pi/2^-} \\tan x"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- As $x \\to \\pi/2^-$, $\\tan x \\to +\\infty$\n- As $x \\to \\pi/2^+$, $\\tan x \\to -\\infty$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "45", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Show that a vertical asymptote exists at $x=0$ for $f(x) = 1/x$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- One-sided limits: $\\lim_{x\\to 0^+} 1/x = +\\infty$, $\\lim_{x\\to 0^-} 1/x = -\\infty$\n- Since at least one one-sided limit goes to $\\pm\\infty$, $x=0$ is a vertical asymptote."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "46", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate the following limit:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{5x+1}{x^2}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- Split: $\\frac{5x+1}{x^2} = \\frac{5x}{x^2} + \\frac{1}{x^2} = \\frac{5}{x} + \\frac{1}{x^2}$\n- As $x \\to 0^+$, $\\frac{5}{x} + \\frac{1}{x^2} \\to +\\infty$\n- As $x \\to 0^-$, $\\frac{5}{x} + \\frac{1}{x^2} \\to -\\infty + \\infty = +\\infty$ (dominant term $1/x^2$)\n- So, $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{5x+1}{x^2} = +\\infty$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "47", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate the following limit:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to -1^+} \\frac{2}{x+1}, \\quad \\lim_{x \\to -1^-} \\frac{2}{x+1}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n- As $x \\to -1^+$, $x+1>0 \\implies \\frac{2}{x+1} \\to +\\infty$\n- As $x \\to -1^-$, $x+1<0 \\implies \\frac{2}{x+1} \\to -\\infty$"}]}]}, {"id": "21.14", "title": "Limits at Infinity", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "By limits at infinity, we study the behavior of functions as $x$ becomes very large:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} f(x) \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} f(x)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "These limits may also be $\\infty$ or $-\\infty$."}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Fact 1: Constant over Power", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $r > 0$ is rational and $c$ is a constant:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\frac{c}{x^r} = 0, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} \\frac{c}{x^r} = 0 \\quad (\\text{if } x^r \\text{ defined for } x<0)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Explanation:</b> As $x \\to \\infty$, $x^r$ grows, making the fraction approach 0. The sign of $c$ only affects the approach from above or below."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Fact 2: Polynomials at Infinity", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "For $p(x) = a_n x^n + \\dots + a_0$, degree $n$, $a_n \\neq 0$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} p(x) = \\lim_{x \\to \\infty} a_n x^n, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} p(x) = \\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} a_n x^n"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Explanation:</b> Highest-degree term dominates; lower-degree terms are negligible."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Horizontal Asymptote", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A function $f(x)$ has a horizontal asymptote at $y = L$ if:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} f(x) = L \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} f(x) = L"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Explanation:</b> The graph approaches $y=L$ as $x$ moves far from the origin."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "48", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} (2x^4 - x^2 - 8x), \\quad\n\\lim_{t \\to -\\infty} \\left(\\frac{1}{3} t^5 + 2 t^3 - t^2 + 8 \\right)"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} (2x^4 - x^2 - 8x) = \\infty$ (dominant $2x^4$)."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{t \\to -\\infty} (\\frac{1}{3} t^5 + \\dots) = -\\infty$ (dominant $\\frac{1}{3}t^5$ negative)."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "49", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\pm \\infty} \\frac{2x^4 - x^2 + 8x}{-5x^4 + 7}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Factor $x^4$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\frac{2 - 1/x^2 + 8/x^3}{-5 + 7/x^4} \\to -\\frac{2}{5} \\quad \\text{as } x \\to \\pm \\infty"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "50", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\frac{\\sqrt{3x^2 + 6}}{5 - 2x}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} \\frac{\\sqrt{3x^2 + 6}}{5 - 2x}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$x \\to \\infty: \\frac{\\sqrt{x^2(3 + 6/x^2)}}{x(-2 + 5/x)} \\to -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$x \\to -\\infty: \\frac{-x\\sqrt{3 + 6/x^2}}{x(-2 + 5/x)} \\to \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Exponential Function Behavior", "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} e^x = \\infty, \\quad \n\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} e^x = 0, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} e^{-x} = 0, \\quad \n\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} e^{-x} = \\infty"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "51", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} e^{2 - 4x - 8x^2} = 0, \\quad\n\\lim_{t \\to -\\infty} e^{t^4 - 5 t^2 + 1} = \\infty, \\quad\n\\lim_{z \\to 0^+} e^{1/z} = \\infty"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "52", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\left(e^{10x} - 4 e^{6x} + \\dots \\right) = \\infty, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} \\left(e^{10x} - 4 e^{6x} + \\dots \\right) = -\\infty"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Logarithmic Function Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} \\ln x = -\\infty, \\quad \\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\ln x = \\infty"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "53", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\ln(7x^3 - x^2 + 1) = \\infty, \\quad\n\\lim_{t \\to -\\infty} \\ln(t^2 - 5t) = \\infty"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Inverse Tangent Function Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\tan^{-1} x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\quad \n\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} \\tan^{-1} x = -\\frac{\\pi}{2}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "54", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\tan^{-1} x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} \\tan^{-1} x = -\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\tan^{-1}(x^3 - 5x + 6) = \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\quad\n\\lim_{x \\to 0^-} \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) = -\\frac{\\pi}{2}"}]}]}, {"id": "21.15", "title": "Limit Formulas", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "formulas", "name": "Formulas", "num": null, "title": "Basic Limit Properties", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to a} c = c$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to a} x = a$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to a} \\big(f(x) \\pm g(x)\\big) = \\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) \\pm \\lim_{x \\to a} g(x)$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to a} \\big(f(x) g(x)\\big) = \\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) \\cdot \\lim_{x \\to a} g(x)$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to a} \\dfrac{f(x)}{g(x)} = \\dfrac{\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)}{\\lim_{x \\to a} g(x)}, \\; g(a)\\neq 0$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "formulas", "name": "Formulas", "num": null, "title": "Limits Involving Infinity (Rational Functions)", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\dfrac{a_n x^n + \\cdots}{b_m x^m + \\cdots} =\n\\begin{cases}\n0, & n < m \\\\\n\\dfrac{a_n}{b_m}, & n = m \\\\\n\\infty \\text{ or } -\\infty, & n > m\n\\end{cases}$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to a^-} \\dfrac{1}{x-a} = -\\infty$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to a^+} \\dfrac{1}{x-a} = +\\infty$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "formulas", "name": "Formulas", "num": null, "title": "Standard Trigonometric Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{x} = 1$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\tan x}{x} = 1$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{1 - \\cos x}{x^2} = \\dfrac{1}{2}$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "formulas", "name": "Formulas", "num": null, "title": "Exponential and Logarithmic Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{e^x - 1}{x} = 1$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\ln(1+x)}{x} = 1$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\left(1 + \\dfrac{1}{x}\\right)^x = e$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} x^n \\ln x = 0 \\quad (n>0)$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\dfrac{\\ln x}{x} = 0$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\dfrac{x^n}{e^x} = 0$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "formulas", "name": "Formulas", "num": null, "title": "Inverse Trigonometric Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\arctan x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} \\arctan x = -\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\arcsin x}{x} = 1$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\arctan x}{x} = 1$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "formulas", "name": "Formulas", "num": null, "title": "L'Hospital's Rule", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $\\lim_{x \\to a} \\dfrac{f(x)}{g(x)}$ is $\\dfrac{0}{0}$ or $\\dfrac{\\infty}{\\infty}$, then"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} \\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} = \\lim_{x \\to a} \\frac{f'(x)}{g'(x)}, \\quad \\text{if the limit exists.}"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "formulas", "name": "Formulas", "num": null, "title": "Squeeze Theorem", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $f(x) \\le g(x) \\le h(x)$ and\n$\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = \\lim_{x \\to a} h(x) = L$, then\n$\\lim_{x \\to a} g(x) = L$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "formulas", "name": "Formulas", "num": null, "title": "Other Useful Limits", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} x^x = 1$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\left(1 + \\frac{k}{x}\\right)^{mx} = e^{km}, \\quad k,m \\in \\mathbb{R}$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} e^{-x} = 0$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} e^x = 0$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} e^x = \\infty$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} e^{-x} = \\infty$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "55", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 2} (3x^2 + 5x - 1)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Using the sum and constant multiple properties of limits:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 2} (3x^2 + 5x - 1) = 3 \\lim_{x \\to 2} x^2 + 5 \\lim_{x \\to 2} x - 1 = 3(4) + 5(2) -1 = 21"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "56", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to -1} \\frac{x^3 + 1}{x+1}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Factor numerator: $x^3+1=(x+1)(x^2-x+1)$"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to -1} \\frac{(x+1)(x^2-x+1)}{x+1} = \\lim_{x \\to -1} (x^2-x+1) = 3"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "57", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sqrt{x+4} - 2}{x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Rationalize the numerator:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}+2}{\\sqrt{x+4}+2} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+4}+2} \\implies \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{4}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "58", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{x^2-1}{x-1}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Factor numerator: $x^2-1=(x-1)(x+1)$"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{x-1} = \\lim_{x \\to 1} (x+1) = 2"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "59", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{1-\\cos x}{x^2}$ using $1-\\cos x = 2\\sin^2(x/2)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{2\\sin^2(x/2)}{x^2} = \\lim_{x \\to 0} 2 \\left(\\frac{\\sin(x/2)}{x}\\right)^2 = 2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{2}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "60", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 4} \\sqrt{x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Using the root property:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 4} \\sqrt{x} = \\sqrt{\\lim_{x \\to 4} x} = 2"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "61", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin 3x}{x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Factor 3:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin 3x}{x} = 3 \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin 3x}{3x} = 3(1) = 3"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "62", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\tan x}{x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Standard limit property:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\tan x}{x} = 1"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "63", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{x^4-1}{x-1}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Factor numerator: $x^4-1 = (x-1)(x^3+x^2+x+1)$"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{(x-1)(x^3+x^2+x+1)}{x-1} = \\lim_{x \\to 1} (x^3+x^2+x+1) = 4"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "64", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{x^2-4}{x^2+4}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Factor numerator: $x^2-4=(x-2)(x+2)$"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{(x-2)(x+2)}{x^2+4} = \\frac{4}{8} = \\frac{1}{2}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "65", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{e^x-1}{x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Standard exponential limit:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{e^x-1}{x} = 1"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "66", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\ln(1+x)}{x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Standard logarithmic limit:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\ln(1+x)}{x} = 1"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "67", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{\\sqrt{x}-1}{x-1}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Rationalize numerator:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-1}{x-1} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x}+1}{\\sqrt{x}+1} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+1} \\implies \\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{2}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "68", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin x + \\tan x}{x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Split limit:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin x}{x} + \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\tan x}{x} = 1 + 1 = 2"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "69", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} \\ln x$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> As $x \\to 0^+$, $\\ln x \\to -\\infty$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "70", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\frac{3x^2+2}{5x^2-7}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Divide numerator and denominator by $x^2$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\frac{3+2/x^2}{5-7/x^2} = \\frac{3}{5}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "71", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{1}{x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Limit does not exist; as $x \\to 0^+$, it $\\to \\infty$; as $x \\to 0^-$, it $\\to -\\infty$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "72", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin 2x}{\\sin 3x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Rewrite:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{2x}{3x} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin 2x/(2x)}{\\sin 3x/(3x)} = \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot 1 = \\frac{2}{3}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "73", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 1} (x^5 - 1)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Direct substitution:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 1} (x^5-1) = 1-1=0"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "74", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{e^{2x}-1}{\\sin x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Split and use standard limits:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{e^{2x}-1}{x} \\cdot \\frac{x}{\\sin x} = 2 \\cdot 1 = 2"}]}]}], "sectionCount": 15}